00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.060
- [Instructor] A series of events called

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.970
the menstrual cycle happens
about once every month

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.960
to prepare a woman's body for pregnancy.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.070
Changing levels of natural chemicals

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.040
in the bloodstream called
hormones control these events.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.290
The reproductive organs
affected by these hormones

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.003
include the vagina,

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.313
cervix,

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.453
uterus,

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.923
fallopian tubes,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.300
and ovaries.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.850
The ovaries produce two main hormones

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.593
called estrogen and progesterone.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.530
As the level of estrogen begins to rise,

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.810
It causes the normally thick mucus

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.253
inside the cervix to thin out.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.170
Estrogen also triggers other hormones

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.083
to cause one of the
ovaries to release an egg.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.493
This process is called ovulation.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.860
If a woman has sex during this time,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.710
a man's reproductive cells called sperm

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.303
can pass through the thinner
mucus to fertilize an egg.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.600
In the uterus, estrogen
causes the lining to thicken

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.763
which prepares it to
receive a fertilized egg.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.670
Rising progesterone levels

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.830
cause glands in the
lining to release fluid

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.933
that feeds the fertilized egg.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.120
Progesterone also causes

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.450
the thinned out mucus in the cervix

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.110
to become thick again,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.653
which prevents sperm from passing through.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.440
If an egg hasn't been fertilized

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.583
the levels of both estrogen
progesterone begin to fall.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.890
This drop in hormone
levels causes menstruation,

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.200
a process where the uterus
sheds its inner tissue lining

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.253
and blood through the vagina.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.750
A progestin implant is a form

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.020
of birth control or a contraception.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.943
It prevents pregnancy
for up to three years.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.180
The device is implanted

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.610
under the skin in a woman's upper arm.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.130
A progestin implant is

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:33.130
a matchstick size flexible plastic rod

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:37.173
containing a progesterone-like
hormone called progestin.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.163
It's designed to be able
to show up on x-rays.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:48.233
The implant continually
releases progestin in the body.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:51.580
High progestin levels
help prevent the body

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.223
from releasing other hormones
that cause ovulation.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.710
Without ovulation,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.540
there is no egg available
for fertilization,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.463
so a woman can't get pregnant.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.270
A second way progestin prevents pregnancy

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:10.390
involves its effect on
the mucus in the cervix.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.110
High progestin levels keep

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.440
the mucus in the cervix thick enough

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.433
so sperm can't get through it.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.160
A third way progestin prevents pregnancy

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.800
involve its influence on
the lining of the uterus.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.500
In contrast to natural progesterone,

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.980
progestin is slightly
different chemically.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:31.840
Over time,

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.150
it makes the uterine lining
thinner instead of thicker.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.050
As a result, if fertilization
of an egg does take place

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.620
the lining may be too thin
for it to stay in the uterus,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.633
so it passes out of the body
with the next menstrual period.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.680
A doctor can insert a progestin implant

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.600
during an office visit.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.450
To do this,

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.010
the doctor will make two
marks with a sterile marker.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.270
One for the insertion site,
and a second mark used

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.923
as a direction guide during insertion.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:10.290
Then the insertion area will
be cleaned with an antiseptic

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.683
and numbed with a local anesthetic.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.240
Next, the doctor will
use a special applicator

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.010
to puncture the skin with a hollow needle

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.573
containing the implant and
slide it beneath the skin.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.760
Finally, the needle will be removed

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.713
leaving implant behind.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.850
After the implant is placed

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.090
the doctor will ensure proper placement

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:38.883
by feeling for both ends of
the implant under the skin.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.223
A bandage will be placed
over the insertion site.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.240
Menstrual bleeding with
a progestin implant

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.400
may include changes in bleeding frequency,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.563
bleeding intensity, and duration
of each bleeding period.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.460
Although the implant can be removed sooner

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.003
it must be removed after three years.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.723
A doctor can replace it with
a new implant at that time.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.560
If pregnancy is suspected, it's important

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.950
for a woman to see her
healthcare provider.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.613
The implant may need to be moved.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.680
A progestin implant is

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.610
over 99% effective at
preventing pregnancy.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:25.370
This means less than 1 out of 100 women

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.010
will become pregnant each year

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.440
using this form of birth control.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:32.260
For more information on
any type of birth control

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.113
talk to your healthcare provider.

